  "description": "Turks and Caicos National Insurance Board contributions for 2026. Covers private sector employees (5.5% employee and 6.5% employer on insurable earnings up to USD 4,000 a month), public officers, the self-employed rate of 11% of elected weekly income from 1 April 2026 under Legal Notice 3 of 2026 and its new payment window, voluntary contributors at 10%, registration from age 16 to 65, the monthly payment and grace period, and the online payment portal. Trigger phrases include NIB contributions, Turks and Caicos national insurance, TCI social security, NIB self-employed 11%.",
